# Hand process 1 over to the real iOS launchd.
#
# Why from /redwood and not /sbin/launchd.ios: the system volume (md0) is the
# root, but a pid 1 execve() of a file on it fails in namei even though the same
# binary runs fine when forked and even though 7-Zip extracts it by path. The
# small root image (md1, /redwood) has no such problem -- exec of
# /redwood/bin/child from pid 1 works -- so the same binary is carried there.
#
# init has already mounted /private/var (ramfs) and created its directories, and
# stage0 has bound /redwood/LaunchDaemons onto /System/Library/LaunchDaemons and
# /redwood/xpc onto /System/Library/xpc, so launchd reads the job cache that
# mkcache.py wrote (launchd_unsecure_cache=1 skips its signature check).
#
# Register the Metal plugin before launchd hands out renderers (v93 semantics,
# dropped in the v94/v95 restructure and back as of v102: without this line
# SpringBoard takes two SIGSEGVs per round once the glass/icon work runs --
# v100 restored it and the round went crash-free).
/redwood/bin/metal_props on ../../../redwood/lib/RedwoodMetal RedwoodMetalDevice
exec /redwood/sbin/launchd.ios
